  <h2>1. Definitions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>NeedleBase / the Service</strong>: the NeedleBase software for tailors, seamstresses, dressmakers and fashion workshop owners, including the Android app, the website, and the application programming interface (API) that syncs them.</li>
    <li><strong>Business</strong>: a tailoring or fashion workshop that registers for NeedleBase.</li>
    <li><strong>Owner</strong>: the person who registers a Business and controls its account. <strong>Staff</strong>: people the Business authorises under roles such as Owner, Manager or Tailor.</li>
    <li><strong>Business Data</strong>: information entered by or for a Business, including customer records, body measurements, sewing orders and payment records.</li>
    <li><strong>Licence key</strong>: a key issued for a Business that allows it to use the Service, and that may carry a plan, a trial or complimentary period, or an expiry date.</li>
    <li><strong>Personal data</strong> has the meaning in the Data Protection Act, 2012 (Act 843): data about an individual who can be identified from that data, or from that data and other information.</li>
